flashinfer: VLLM_FLASHINFER_SM75=1 opts Turing (sm75) back into the FlashInfer backend.

The floor was raised to sm80 for flashinfer issue #3620 (prefill launches over the 64 KB
shared-memory limit). It stays sm80 by default; the env var lowers it to sm75 for an
explicit --attention-backend FLASHINFER. Triton 3.7 emits no tensor-core code on sm75,
so FlashInfer's CUDA kernels are the tensor-core attention path there.

Verified on 2x RTX 2080 Ti (flashinfer 0.7.0.post1, fp16, TP=2, DFlash2): boots, greedy
output matches TRITON_ATTN, 24k-token prompt decodes at 91-93 tok/s (74 on Triton) and
prefills in 16 s cold (80 s on Triton).

Kind: local
What: VLLM_FLASHINFER_SM75=1 opts sm75 (Turing) back into the FlashInfer backend, the tensor-core attention path there
Upstream: none (flashinfer issue #3620 raised the floor to sm80)
Cut-against: 0.33.0
Retires-when: FlashInfer supports sm75 prefill within shared-memory limits

